Multi-model side-by-side mode — load YOLO26n and the fine-tuned MobileNetV2 ELU at the same time and display both decisions on the overlay. Demonstrates your best two models simultaneously and lets you answer "why YOLO over MobileNet?" live.

Session evidence log — auto-write a demo_session_<timestamp>.json + demo_session_<timestamp>.md containing every decision (timestamp, model, class, confidence, latency, capture path). At end-of-session, print a summary table (total frames, PASS count, FAIL count, mean latency, mean confidence). This gives you the "saved examples of live PASS/FAIL decisions" the rubric wants.

Hotkeys for the demo flow:

SPACE — capture & log a frame manually (good for the moment when you hold up an unseen cup)
g then 1/2 — assert ground truth (PASS/FAIL) → running accuracy displayed
p — pause inference
q — quit + write summary
Medium-impact
Better overlay — probability bar for both classes, FPS counter, running PASS/FAIL counts, model name. Currently shows only top-1 confidence.

Confidence threshold flag — --confidence-threshold 0.6 so low-confidence frames show "UNCERTAIN" rather than forcing a binary call. Useful talking point on model limitations.

Auto-detect model type — handle both *.pt YOLO weights and PyTorch state_dicts (your MobileNetV2 checkpoints) without separate scripts.

Graceful missing-model handling — current script crashes hard. Print available models in runs/ and exit cleanly.
